## Findings
1. advisory — brief:43 The claim that `.sidebar { box-sizing: border-box }` "holds the approved 390×48 outer box" is false. `.sidebar` is a stretched grid item with no width or height of its own, so its outer box is already 390×48 without the declaration. The prototype's own b3-red served run (browser-b3-red-W-415-b3.out) passes the 390-width and 48-height rows and fails only at the computed `boxSizing` check, and kill-b3.patch removes only that line. So b3's red pins a declared property, not a geometry failure, and the policy message "the converted wordmark control cannot enlarge the approved navigation box" describes a failure that doesn't occur. Replace with: "`.sidebar { box-sizing: border-box }` is defensive: the stretched grid item already holds 390×48 without it (the b3-red served run passes the width/height rows), so b3's red pins the declared box model, not a geometry change." Rename the b3 policy and served messages to "the phone navigation declares border-box geometry". [severity: S2] [class: tests×assertion-satisfied-by-the-wrong-cause] — check: apps/web/tests-serve/w415.spec.ts
2. advisory — brief:53 "only Board's named phase strip may overflow horizontally" promises more than b2 measures. b2 measures only the expanded state, and only screen roots and document/body. Inner scroll containers (`.inbox__list` and `.inbox__detail`, whose `overflow-y: auto` computes `overflow-x: auto`, and `.shell__main` itself) clip their own overflow, so a root's scrollWidth never sees it. Screen edges are also never measured while collapsed. Replace with: "…at 1280 and 640 CSS px, in the expanded state, every screen root and the document/body right edge stay inside the viewport and no page-level horizontal scroll appears; Board's phase strip is the one named local scroller — limit: descendant scroll containers other than Board's phase strip, the collapsed state's screen edges (only the Seats bar is measured there), open drawers, …(existing limits)". [severity: S2] [class: tests×ruled-case-uncovered] — check: none: a b2 served assertion over every computed `overflow-x: auto|scroll|hidden` descendant (scrollWidth ≤ clientWidth except `.board__columns`), repeated with the sidebar collapsed
3. advisory — brief:41 "Focus uses the ruled 2px verdigris ring" does not fully hold at 390. The phone `.sidebar` is a 48px flex row at y=0 with no vertical padding, so the toggle stretches to y=0..48. Its 2px ring at 2px offset then has its top edge at y=−4..−2, off-screen. DIRECTION.md §5 requires the ring on every focusable element. Replace with: "Focus uses the ruled 2px verdigris ring at 2px offset; at ≤599px `.sidebar__toggle` is `align-self: center` with the wordmark's vertical padding removed, so all four ring sides stay inside the 48px row." [severity: S2] [class: tests×ruled-case-uncovered] — check: none: a b1 served assertion at 390 that the focused toggle's box top is ≥ 4 and its bottom is ≤ 44
4. advisory — brief:74 Input-domain row 2's "Rejected by" names `window.innerWidth`, media-query computed layout and rendered rectangles. None of these is a rejecting function; the served row's `expect()` calls are. Replace the cell with: "`expect(await page.evaluate(() => window.innerWidth)).toBe(width)` and `expect()` on rendered rectangles reject the first mismatched ruled input". [severity: S4] [class: spec×input-without-named-rejector] — check: none: a spec-admission rule that each Rejected-by cell names a function that throws or fails
5. advisory — brief:51 "the main pane receives released left-rail width" is stated for 1280, 640 and 390, but at 390 there is no left rail and main keeps the full width (brief:99). Replace with: "…and at 1280 and 640 the main pane receives the released left-rail width, while at 390 it keeps the full viewport width, as pinned by…". [severity: S4] [class: spec×prose-contradiction-under-revision] — check: apps/web/tests-serve/w415.spec.ts

